00:19:11.601 --> 00:19:13.133
-Yeah, of course.

00:19:13.133 --> 00:19:14.901
-Are people gonna like
flip on and think that's real?

00:19:14.901 --> 00:19:16.234
-Yeah, of course.
-Great.

00:19:16.234 --> 00:19:17.968
-That's fun.
[ Laughter ]

00:19:17.968 --> 00:19:19.767
You always come on
and do a fun bit.

00:19:19.767 --> 00:19:21.868
And then we'll get
to the real meat and potatoes

00:19:21.868 --> 00:19:23.801
of the interview here.
It's "Ant-Man,"

00:19:23.801 --> 00:19:26.601
"Ant-Man and the Wasp:
Quantumania."

00:19:26.601 --> 00:19:28.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
I saw it.

00:19:28.501 --> 00:19:30.033
It is fantastic.
It is giant.

00:19:30.033 --> 00:19:31.834
-Thank you, yeah.
-It's massive.

00:19:31.834 --> 00:19:34.534
I mean, is it --
I don't know.

00:19:34.534 --> 00:19:38.334
Is it tough to be involved
in a set that's all CGI?

00:19:38.334 --> 00:19:41.133
-There were some days there was
the thing called volume.

00:19:41.133 --> 00:19:43.100
And some days we would film
and people said,

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:44.400
[ Whispering ]
"You know, we're going to film
the volume."

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:47.634
And the volume is
a new technology.

00:19:47.634 --> 00:19:49.067
You know, normally you're
shooting with bluescreens

00:19:49.067 --> 00:19:51.167
all around you,
but it's this --

00:19:51.167 --> 00:19:52.934
it's like an LED screen
that wraps

00:19:52.934 --> 00:19:54.901
around an entire sound stage.

00:19:54.901 --> 00:19:59.133
And so they try and make it feel
as much like the quantum realm

00:19:59.133 --> 00:20:01.968
or whatever and we have
something to react to.

00:20:01.968 --> 00:20:03.934
And it was crazy
to go into these sound stages

00:20:03.934 --> 00:20:07.234
and it looked like you were
in outer space, something wild.

00:20:07.234 --> 00:20:08.834
-And what is the ground like?
Is it the ground --

00:20:08.834 --> 00:20:10.767
-They put on dirt.
They like have dirt

00:20:10.767 --> 00:20:12.801
and they try and have as much
practical stuff as possible.

00:20:12.801 --> 00:20:14.767
-So you really feel like you're
on a planet or whatever.

00:20:14.767 --> 00:20:16.501
-You really feel like you're
on a planet

00:20:16.501 --> 00:20:18.868
or you're in some weird space.

00:20:18.868 --> 00:20:20.334
One of the things that --
Actually, we went in

00:20:20.334 --> 00:20:22.434
and there was dirt all
over the floor

00:20:22.434 --> 00:20:26.968
and we were shooting with like
150 other creatures and people

00:20:26.968 --> 00:20:30.267
and it doesn't smell good
at all.

00:20:30.267 --> 00:20:32.334
[ Laughter ]
"Mm."

00:20:32.334 --> 00:20:33.434
And then throughout the day,

00:20:33.434 --> 00:20:34.634
it was kind of getting worse
and worse.

00:20:34.634 --> 00:20:36.868
The next day,
it was like overbearing

00:20:36.868 --> 00:20:39.667
and we realized they probably
got a deal on the dirt

00:20:39.667 --> 00:20:42.067
because it actually wasn't dirt.
It was manure.

00:20:42.067 --> 00:20:43.434
[ Ohhs and laughter ]

00:20:43.434 --> 00:20:44.567
-What?!

00:20:44.567 --> 00:20:46.133
Are you kidding me?
-No.

00:20:46.133 --> 00:20:48.000
-Wow!
-They actually had to kind of

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.667
shut it down for a day
and then bring in some new dirt.

00:20:50.667 --> 00:20:53.634
I don't think anyone knew
and it was --

00:20:53.634 --> 00:20:56.667
-You'd think manure would be
more expensive than dirt.

00:20:56.667 --> 00:20:57.934
-Apparently not.
-Apparently not!

00:20:57.934 --> 00:21:00.801
-Yeah. Yeah. Yeah,
the quantum realm just reeks.

00:21:00.801 --> 00:21:03.133
-Wow! I did not know that.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:21:03.133 --> 00:21:06.334
-Paul, how do we set up
this film?

00:21:06.334 --> 00:21:08.968
I would say it's just
action adventure comedy.

